From bb8e6307c65d5f281230e35105cee9a2661e0888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:10:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/85] aegisos: refresh lockscreen multi-user avatar
 visibility on enabled-state change
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

KeyguardStatusBarView#setUserSwitcherEnabled() stored the new value but
never re-applied it — the avatar's actual visibility is only touched by
updateVisibilities(), called elsewhere (setVisibility(VISIBLE), the
keyguard-avatar/switcher enabled setters) but not from here. In stock
AOSP this was invisible because isUserSwitcherEnabled() never changed
within a keyguard's lifetime; AegisOS Duress Unlock's decoy session is
the first caller whose answer changes live, mid-session, exposing a
race against KeyguardStatusBarViewController#updateUserSwitcher()'s
async UserManager call — the avatar kept showing the pre-switch state
during real hardware validation of patch 0033.

Call updateVisibilities() directly so the view updates the moment the
new value arrives, instead of waiting on an unrelated visibility event.
---
 .../systemui/statusbar/phone/KeyguardStatusBarView.java    | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/KeyguardStatusBarView.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/KeyguardStatusBarView.java
index 13cfa806496d..900fbb1be4d8 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/KeyguardStatusBarView.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/KeyguardStatusBarView.java
@@ -188,6 +188,13 @@ public class KeyguardStatusBarView extends RelativeLayout {
 
     public void setUserSwitcherEnabled(boolean enabled) {
         mIsUserSwitcherEnabled = enabled;
+        // Without this, a change is only applied the next time updateVisibilities() happens to
+        // run for an unrelated reason (e.g. this view's own setVisibility(VISIBLE)), which can
+        // race behind the async UserManager call in
+        // KeyguardStatusBarViewController#updateUserSwitcher() and leave mMultiUserAvatar
+        // showing a stale state — including across an AegisOS Duress Unlock decoy switch, whose
+        // whole point is that isUserSwitcherEnabled()'s answer changes mid-session.
+        updateVisibilities();
     }
 
     private void updateKeyguardStatusBarHeight() {
